OL,4,CProblem drinking divides England
OL,5, There are stark geographical divisions
OL,6, in the toll alcohol takes on health in
OL,7, England, with men in the North West
OL,8, more likely to die prematurely than
OL,9, those in the South East, figures show.
OL,11,FData collected by the North West Public
OL,12,FHealth Observatory shows almost 16,000
OL,13,Fpeople died in England last year as a
OL,14,Fresult of alcohol-related harm.
OL,16,FTwo-thirds of the areas with the
OL,17,Fhighest harm levels were in the North.
OL,19,FBut alcohol-attributable crime was at
OL,20,Fits peak in London.
OL,22,D]C This Ceefax page is from 01-09-10
OL,23,S]D Much more at: teletextarchive.com
